      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "Kleinias has answered that it is the clever who learn. But Euthydemos now\nexploits an ambiguity in the terms 'clever', 'ignorant', 'learner': a man may be\nclever either because he has learnt something, or because he is able to learn it. The\nsame word covers both cases, and this gives Euthydemos room to manoeuvre.",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
